{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And the melakhah</b> Three times in the Masorah: והמלאכה היתה דים. והמלאכה לא ליום אחד ולשנים בעזרא. והמלאכה גדולה בדברי הימים in the matter of building the House — even though the melakhah was great, not for one day and not for two, even so it was דים (sufficient), for a blessing was sent in the work of their hands." "<b>דים</b> Three times in the Masorah: היתה דים · הלא יגנבו דים · אם גנבים בלילה השחיתו דים. In the overthrow of Edom, in Edom it is said 'they' — 'build up and I will tear down'; but in Jacob — והמלאכה היתה דים." "<b>And it was left over</b> Three times: here, and the other כי כה אמר ה׳ אכול והותר, and מהחל התרומה להביא בית ה׳ אכול ושבוע והותר in דברי הימים ב. In the merit of Torah and the Holy Temple, blessing comes as satiety to the world, as written: למן היום אשר יוסד היכל ה׳ וגו׳ עד מן היום הזה אברך."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {1 "The phrase 'בנו ואני אהרוס' appears to quote Obadiah 1:3-4 (Edom's boast); the juxtaposition with Jacob's 'דים' is the Ba'al HaTurim's own reading across the three occurrences. The text is terse and possibly corrupt; translated hyper-literally.", 2 "The third occurrence is cited as being in דה\"ב (2 Chronicles 31:10); the 'ג׳' count includes our verse plus the two named citations. The phrase 'והותד' appears to be a typographical error for 'והותר'; translated as 'והותר' based on context."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:15:17.674696693Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}